class_name DriftSky
extends Node3D
## The world round a Marble Drift course: the courses float high in the sky (or in space) like shiny toy tracks,
## with an abyss far below so a fall feels deep. One theme per course (DriftCourse.theme, 0-5):
##   0 Dawn Isles     a gold dawn over a sea of cloud, floating grassy islands with trees, cloud banks
##   1 Nebula Reach   deep space: a nebula band and stars all round, a ringed gas giant and moons below, a drifting
##                    asteroid belt circling under the course
##   2 Crystal Hollow a dark cavern: giant glowing crystal clusters rising out of violet mist, floating shards
##   3 Neon Run       a synthwave sunset: a striped sun, a scrolling neon grid far below, wireframe mountains,
##                    floating neon shapes
##   4 Storm Front    a slate sky over thunderclouds: lightning flickering inside them and bolts down into them,
##                    dark floating rocks, rain
##   5 Polar Night    stars and aurora curtains over a frozen cloud sea, tall glowing ice spires
## Everything is made here from code and the shaders in ../shaders (our own designs, CC BY-SA 4.0; no third-party
## assets, nothing generated by a model).
##
## API: build(theme, course_size) makes the diorama (course_size: the course's width, height range and length; the
## course lies in x 0..W, z 0..H with floors near y 0..12). environment_for(theme) gives PopBackdrop's environment
## keys plus sky_material (the sky shader, also used for reflections), fog_height, fog_height_density, name; the view
## calls make_environment(d) and setup_sun(light, d). palette(theme) gives the course shaders' colours and
## course_materials(theme) two ready ShaderMaterials [top, side]. The abyss layers, rain and motes follow the
## current camera; everything animates in _process on the node's own clock (fixed-step safe, deterministic).

